  "delivered_messages_sha256": "b16a71ebc6be772fc2271cc8ac6fffeb23cc33dd70ffb78e451baf6db674505f",
  "raw_text": "No. Timing alone establishes correlation, not causation.\n\nThe update may be responsible, but proving causation requires additional evidence, such as:\n\n- Reproducing the failure after installing the update\n- Identifying a plausible mechanism linking the update to the breakdown\n- Reviewing logs or diagnostics\n- Ruling out hardware wear, operator error, power issues, or other changes\n- Showing the problem disappears after rollback or recurs on reinstallation\n\nSo the one-day sequence raises suspicion and justifies investigation, but does not by itself establish causation.",
